---
// The homepage. Its Markdown twin for agents is src/homepage.md (served as /index.md and at the top of
// /llms-full.txt): change both together. Adapted from Fleetlayer's homepage (Apache 2.0, see NOTICE): its layout and
// classes, with Quietdeck's content. The Inbox pictures are HTML (src/styles/inbox-mock.css) with made-up mail.
import "../styles/home.css";
import "../styles/inbox-mock.css";
import mark from "../assets/mark.svg?raw";
import { site, repo } from "../../site.config.mjs";
const title = "Quietdeck: clear your inbox in one pass, and let your agents do the work";
const description = site.summary;
const chat = `<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M21 15a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H7l-4 4V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h14a2 2 0 0 1 2 2z"/></svg>`;
const mail = `<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="2" y="4" width="20" height="16" rx="2"/><path d="m22 7-10 6L2 7"/></svg>`;
const check = `<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg>`;
const done = `<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="11" fill="currentColor"/><path d="m7 12.5 3.2 3L17 9" fill="none" stroke="oklch(18% 0.02 250)" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>`;
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>{title}</title>
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
    <link rel="canonical" href={site.url + "/"} />
    <link rel="alternate" type="text/markdown" href="/index.md" title="This page as Markdown" />
    <meta property="og:title" content={title} />
    <meta property="og:description" content={description} />
    <meta property="og:url" content={site.url + "/"} />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <!-- Privacy-friendly analytics by Plausible -->
    <script async src="https://pa.docspring.com/js/pa-WWnRAMt1H8HtDUKNOMPQh.js" is:inline></script>
    <script is:inline>
      window.plausible=window.plausible||function(){(plausible.q=plausible.q||[]).push(arguments)},plausible.init=plausible.init||function(i){plausible.o=i||{}};
      plausible.init()
    </script>
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
    <header class="nav">
      <div class="nav__inner">
        <a class="wordmark" href="/" aria-label="Quietdeck home">
          <span class="wordmark__mark" set:html={mark} />
          <span>Quietdeck</span>
        </a>
        <nav class="nav__links" aria-label="Main">
          <a href="/concepts/">How it works</a>
          <a href="/solo/">Docs</a>
          <a href={repo}>GitHub</a>
        </nav>
        <a class="btn btn--primary nav__cta" href="/solo/">Get started</a>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main id="main">
      <section class="hero hero--stack" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
        <div class="hero__copy">
          <p class="status-line"><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span> Source-available · early · built in public</p>
          <h1 id="hero-title">Clear your inbox in one pass. Your agents do the work.</h1>
          <p class="lede">
            An AI agent reads every email and writes you one page: what needs a decision at the top, everything that can
            just be archived at the bottom. You change what you'd do differently and press Approve All. Work goes to the
            AI session that should handle it, and nothing happens to your mail until you approve it.
          </p>
          <div class="actions">
            <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/solo/">Run it on your computer</a>
            <a class="btn btn--quiet" href="/concepts/">See how it works</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <figure class="mock" aria-label="The Quietdeck Inbox: a report with four numbered items that need a decision, each with a default action, and routine mail grouped under Archive all">
          <div class="mock__nav" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="mock__brand">Quietdeck</span>
            <span class="mock__tab mock__tab--on">Inbox<span class="mock__count">23</span></span>
            <span class="mock__tab">Drafts</span>
            <span class="mock__tab">Threads</span>
            <span class="mock__tab">Sessions</span>
            <span class="mock__tab">History</span>
            <span class="mock__tab">Rules</span>
          </div>
          <div class="mock__body">
            <h4>Inbox</h4>
            <ol>
              <li>
                <b>Northwind Bakery wants annual billing:</b> three emails from the owner and their accountant, the last
                asking for an invoice by Friday. Forward to <code>billing</code> to draft the invoice and your reply.
                <div class="mock__default"><span>Forward to <code>billing</code></span><span class="mock__icons"><Fragment set:html={chat} /><Fragment set:html={mail} /><Fragment set:html={check} /></span></div>
              </li>
              <li>
                <b>CI failed on main (web):</b> two Playwright tests timed out after the <code>web</code> session's push
                at 09:40. Resume <code>web</code>, forward it there, then archive.
                <div class="mock__default"><span>Resume <code>web</code>, forward and archive</span><span class="mock__icons"><Fragment set:html={chat} /><Fragment set:html={mail} /><Fragment set:html={check} /></span></div>
              </li>
              <li>
                <b>Your certificate for sign.example.com is issued.</b> Nothing is set up for it yet. Start a session in
                <code>~/code/certs</code> with this email to install it.
                <div class="mock__default"><span>Start a session: <code>certs</code></span><span class="mock__icons"><Fragment set:html={chat} /><Fragment set:html={mail} /><Fragment set:html={check} /></span></div>
              </li>
              <li>
                <b>Dentist moved your check-up to Thursday 3pm.</b> Reply only if the new time doesn't work.
                <div class="mock__default"><span>Add to calendar, then archive</span><span class="mock__icons"><Fragment set:html={chat} /><Fragment set:html={mail} /><Fragment set:html={check} /></span></div>
              </li>
            </ol>
            <h5>Archive all</h5>
            <ul>
              <li>Hosting: a $24.00 monthly receipt.</li>
              <li>Two directory listings asking for a "no" reply to stop.</li>
              <li>Pull request #142 was merged; <code>web</code> already knows.</li>
              <li>A Black Friday promo from a tool you use.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="mock__bar" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="mock__state">Idle</span>
            <span class="mock__input">Message quietdeck triage</span>
            <span class="mock__approve">Approve All</span>
          </div>
        </figure>
      </section>

      <section class="pain" aria-labelledby="pain-title">
        <h2 id="pain-title">Email is where the work starts</h2>
        <p>
          A customer asks for something, a build fails, an invoice arrives, a vendor says the certificate is ready. Most
          of it is work for an agent, and AI agents are good at that work now. Getting it from your inbox to the right
          agent is still on you.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Gmail's notifications are too noisy, so mail piles up until you get round to it.</li>
          <li>Each email that's really a task means reading it, working out which session should handle it, and pasting it in.</li>
          <li>CI failures and alerts land in your inbox even when an agent is already watching that build.</li>
          <li>You still want to see every receipt, with its amount, before it's archived. Forty emails one at a time takes the entire morning.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="fixes" aria-labelledby="fixes-title">
        <h2 id="fixes-title">One pass, and the work is handed out</h2>
        <ul class="fixes__list">
          <li>
            <p class="fixes__was">forty emails, one at a time</p>
            <h3>One page, decisions first</h3>
            <p>
              What needs you is numbered at the top. Receipts, newsletters and pitches are one line each under Archive
              all. Three emails about the same thing become one item.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <p class="fixes__was">pasting emails into sessions</p>
            <h3>Approve All hands out the work</h3>
            <p>
              Each email goes to the AI session that owns it. Approve All resumes a session that has ended, or
              starts a new one in the right folder, and the agents get on with it.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <p class="fixes__was">approve, then explain what you meant</p>
            <h3>Change anything in plain words</h3>
            <p>
              Open a thread under any item and say what you'd do instead. The agent updates its proposal and waits for
              you again.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <p class="fixes__was">alerts for things agents already handle</p>
            <h3>Alerts go to the agent that owns them</h3>
            <p>
              A service's alerts go straight to its agent, and the report gets a count. An agent watching CI can keep
              those emails out of your inbox while it works.
            </p>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="feature" aria-labelledby="group-title">
        <div class="feature__copy">
          <h2 id="group-title">Three people, one thing, one line</h2>
          <p>
            When several emails are about the same thing, the agent groups them into one item with one decision. The mail
            icon lists every email behind it, with a summary of each and a link to open it in Gmail.
          </p>
        </div>
        <figure class="mock" aria-label="One item grouping three emails from different people about Northwind Bakery's annual billing, with the mail menu open listing all three">
          <div class="mock__body">
            <ol>
              <li>
                <b>Northwind Bakery wants annual billing:</b> three emails from the owner and their accountant, the last
                asking for an invoice by Friday. Forward to <code>billing</code> to draft the invoice and your reply.
                <div class="mock__default"><span>Forward to <code>billing</code></span><span class="mock__icons"><Fragment set:html={chat} /><span class="on"><Fragment set:html={mail} /></span><Fragment set:html={check} /></span></div>
                <div class="mock__menu">
                  <p class="mock__menu-head">3 emails</p>
                  <div class="mock__mail"><span><b>Moving to annual billing</b><small>Priya, Northwind Bakery · Mon</small></span><i>›</i></div>
                  <div class="mock__mail"><span><b>Re: Moving to annual billing</b><small>Sam, their accountant · Tue</small></span><i>›</i></div>
                  <div class="mock__mail"><span><b>Invoice needed by Friday</b><small>Priya, Northwind Bakery · today</small></span><i>›</i></div>
                </div>
              </li>
            </ol>
          </div>
        </figure>
      </section>

      <section class="feature" aria-labelledby="thread-title">
        <div class="feature__copy">
          <h2 id="thread-title">Say what you'd do instead</h2>
          <p>
            Every item has a thread. Type what you want in your own words: a different session, a reply in your tone, keep
            it for later. The agent rewrites the item, and nothing runs until you approve the new version.
          </p>
        </div>
        <figure class="mock" aria-label="A thread under a CI failure item: you ask for it to go to the release session instead, and the triage agent confirms it changed the item">
          <div class="mock__body">
            <ol start="2">
              <li>
                <b>CI failed on main (web):</b> two Playwright tests timed out after the <code>release</code> session's
                push at 09:40. Resume <code>release</code>, forward it there, then archive.
                <div class="mock__thread">
                  <div class="mock__default"><span class="mock__icons mock__done"><Fragment set:html={done} /></span><span>Resume <code>release</code>, forward and archive</span><span class="mock__icons"><span class="on"><Fragment set:html={chat} /></span><Fragment set:html={mail} /></span></div>
                  <p class="mock__msg mock__msg--you">Send this to release, not web. It's their branch.</p>
                  <p class="mock__who mock__who--you">You · 9:52</p>
                  <p class="mock__msg">Changed it to go to release. That session has ended, so approving resumes it, forwards the failure, then archives.</p>
                  <p class="mock__who">quietdeck triage · 9:52</p>
                  <p class="mock__reply">Reply to quietdeck triage</p>
                </div>
              </li>
            </ol>
          </div>
        </figure>
      </section>

      <section class="safe" aria-labelledby="safe-title">
        <h2 id="safe-title">Nothing happens without you seeing it</h2>
        <p>
          The agent proposes, and you approve. Plain code carries out what you approved, exactly as you approved it.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Every archive, label and draft waits on the page until you approve it, and the runner checks the thread hasn't changed since the agent looked.</li>
          <li>Nothing is ever sent. A reply is saved as a Gmail draft for you to edit and send.</li>
          <li>Approve All waits a few seconds with an Undo button, and leaves out anything that changed while you were reading.</li>
          <li>Mail you archive in Gmail yourself drops off the report.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          By default solo's agent is your own Claude Code with full access, so it can read whole threads, your notes and
          the web to work out what each email needs. It reads strangers' mail with that access, and an email written to
          fool it could act as you. A restricted mode limits it to Quietdeck's own command.
        </p>
        <p class="safe__more"><a href="/solo-security/">Quietdeck solo and your security</a></p>
      </section>

      <section class="runs" aria-labelledby="runs-title">
        <h2 id="runs-title">Two ways to run it</h2>
        <div class="runs__grid">
          <div class="runs__card">
            <p class="fixes__was">one computer</p>
            <h3>Quietdeck solo</h3>
            <p>
              One program on your Mac or Linux machine. It reads Gmail through <a href="https://github.com/steipete/gogcli">gog</a>, runs Claude Code as the agent, and
              carries out archives, labels and drafts. Your mail never passes through anyone else's server.
            </p>
            <p><a href="/solo/">Set up solo</a></p>
          </div>
          <div class="runs__card">
            <p class="fixes__was">all your agents</p>
            <h3>A deck on your own server</h3>
            <p>
              The full Quietdeck connects agent sessions on every machine you use. Approve All forwards work to them,
              resumes and starts sessions, and alerts, Matrix rooms and pings on your phone come in too. It's designed to run on{" "}
              <a href="https://fleetlayer.ai">Fleetlayer</a>, but works without it.
            </p>
            <p><a href="/getting-started/">Set up a deck</a></p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="band" aria-labelledby="band-title">
        <div class="band__inner">
          <div class="band__copy">
            <h2 id="band-title">Start on your own computer.</h2>
            <p>
              You need a Mac or a Linux machine, Gmail, <a href="https://github.com/steipete/gogcli">gog</a> and Claude Code. There are no prebuilt releases yet: build
              it from the source in a few minutes, set it up with one command, and it runs as a service from then on.
            </p>
            <p class="band__link"><a href="/solo/">The guide</a></p>
          </div>
          <div class="band__code">
            <p class="band__step">Build it</p>
<pre><code><span class="t-prompt">$</span> git clone {repo}
<span class="t-prompt">$</span> cd quietdeck && pnpm -C web install && pnpm -C web build
<span class="t-prompt">$</span> cargo install --locked --path crates/quietdeck-solo</code></pre>
            <p class="band__step">Set it up and open the Inbox</p>
<pre><code><span class="t-prompt">$</span> quietdeck-solo init && quietdeck-solo install
<span class="t-prompt">$</span> quietdeck-solo open</code></pre>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="state" aria-labelledby="state-title">
        <h2 id="state-title">Where it is today</h2>
        <div class="state__grid">
          <div>
            <h3><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span> Runs now</h3>
            <p>
              Quietdeck solo on macOS and Linux, and the full deck with agents on several machines. The author triages
              their own mail with it every day.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3><span class="dot dot--next" aria-hidden="true"></span> Being built</h3>
            <p>
              Prebuilt releases with a one-line installer, and moving from solo to a deck for many machines without
              starting over.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="state__note">
          Source-available under <a href={`${repo}/blob/main/LICENSE.md`}>FSL-1.1-ALv2</a>: each release becomes Apache
          2.0 two years after it's published. Expect breaking changes.
        </p>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer class="foot">
      <div class="foot__inner">
        <a class="wordmark wordmark--small" href="/"><span class="wordmark__mark" set:html={mark} /><span>Quietdeck</span></a>
        <p>Fair Source (FSL-1.1-ALv2)</p>
        <nav aria-label="Footer">
          <a href="/solo/">Docs</a>
          <a href={repo}>GitHub</a>
          <a href="/llms.txt">llms.txt</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
